<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khana Ratsadon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1927">1927</a>–<a href="/years/1933">1933</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as People's Party (Siam)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khana Ratsadon, or People's Party, was a group of civilian and military officials founded by Thai students in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1927. Led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pridi-banomyong">Pridi Banomyong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plaek-phibunsongkhram">Plaek Phibunsongkhram</a>, it carried out the bloodless revolution of 24 June 1932 that ended absolute monarchy under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prajadhipok">Prajadhipok</a> and introduced Siam's first constitution. Its members dominated Thai politics for the next fifteen years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khana-ratsadon.jpg" alt="Khana Ratsadon" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jo Shigeru · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Memorial_peg_of_Siamese_Revolution_of_2475.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
